From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 00:10:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] ntdll: no JIT pool dump at the first unhandled Mach
 exception

The Mach exception thread wrote the whole JIT pool, 896 MB, to the
Documents folder at the first unhandled exception of the app's life,
which in most runs is a recoverable one (69 of 93 runs on 2026-10-30/31
wrote it). It now does so only with the runtime's diagnostics on
(madeira_diag_enabled).

Linear: PLA-514
Class: diagnostics
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-31-wow-arm64-start.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 build/ntdll-unix/signal_arm64_ios.c | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/build/ntdll-unix/signal_arm64_ios.c b/build/ntdll-unix/signal_arm64_ios.c
index cae8e91..275f47d 100644
--- a/build/ntdll-unix/signal_arm64_ios.c
+++ b/build/ntdll-unix/signal_arm64_ios.c
@@ -5688,9 +5688,14 @@ skip_reclaim_band: ;
                     /* One-shot dump: on the first UNHANDLED exec fault, dump the
                      * JIT-pool RW alias contents around the relevant FEX CodeBuffer
                      * slots to a file. Lets us disassemble FEX-emitted ARM64 offline
-                     * to verify codegen correctness independently. */
+                     * to verify codegen correctness independently.
+                     * Playport (PLA-514): only with the diagnostics on
+                     * (madeira_diag_enabled). The first unhandled fault of most
+                     * runs is a recoverable one, and each wrote the whole pool,
+                     * 896 MB, to the Documents folder (69 of 93 runs on
+                     * 2026-10-30/31). */
                     static volatile int dumped = 0;
-                    if (cnt == 1 && __sync_bool_compare_and_swap(&dumped, 0, 1))
+                    if (cnt == 1 && madeira_diag_enabled && __sync_bool_compare_and_swap(&dumped, 0, 1))
                     {
                         extern void *ios_jit_rw_base_global;
                         extern size_t ios_jit_pool_size_global;
